From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Tue, 30 Jun 2026 17:57:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: 6.18 kernel build compatibility shims

Bridge the API gap that prevents the SmartRG/Adtran Airoha vendor
overlay from building against the 6.18 airoha driver, keeping the
pristine overlay sources unchanged:

- airoha_gdm_dev lost its net_device back-pointer; upstream now uses
  netdev_from_priv(), but the PON offload overlay (arht_dp_api.c and
  related files) reads gdm_dev->dev directly. Restore the member and
  set it at device allocation.

The from_timer()/del_timer() aliases previously carried here were only
needed by arht_dynamic_ifc.c, which the 2026Q2 vendor drop removed.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c |    1 +
 drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h |    1 +
 2 files changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -3977,6 +3977,7 @@ static int airoha_alloc_gdm_device(struc
 
 	netdev->dev.of_node = of_node_get(np);
 	dev = netdev_priv(netdev);
+	dev->dev = netdev;
 	u64_stats_init(&dev->stats.syncp);
 	dev->port = port;
 	dev->eth = eth;
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.h
@@ -671,6 +671,7 @@ struct airoha_gdm_dev {
 	struct airoha_qdma __rcu *qdma;
 	struct airoha_gdm_port *port;
 	struct airoha_eth *eth;
+	struct net_device *dev;
 
 	DECLARE_BITMAP(qos_sq_bmap, AIROHA_NUM_QOS_CHANNELS);
 	/* qos stats counters */
